t their demons are never  exercised  eventually those demons will destroy  them  the supernatural forces at play  naturally parallel the severe mental  illness which runs in the  family demonic possession and curses  after all  have historically been used as  explanations for mental health problems  that could not be otherwise understood  ellen's husband and son both killed  themselves as a result of schizophrenia  or psychotic depression  although her son's claimed that she was  putting voices inside him  raises the question of whether she was  experimenting with demon raising  even back then through these acts of  violence the family's self-destructive  legacy is passed on to each member  dooming them to the same bloody fate as  those who came before  much of who we are is hereditary it's  why so many of us can probably relate to  annie and her family  feeling somewhat doomed to repeat the  past and one day turn into our parents  ultimately the thing which locks the  graham family into their fate isn't  ancient rights or mysterious ruins but  their own inability to process the  trauma they have undergone  they suppress and suppress and suppress  it until it finally  explodes the violence which comes  exploding out  is filled with darkly poetic repetitions  and reversals  annie beheads herself in a gory  imitation of charlie's death  her nighttime fantasies of burning a  family member alive  come true when steve goes up in flames  repression and trauma lock them into a  cycle and their tortured family history  seems doomed to repeat itself  until they have all been destroyed but  what do you guys think are we all doomed  to repeat our family's dysfunction  let us know in the comments big thanks  to our patrons for your support  light that subscribe button on fire and  as always  thanks for watching peace  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  you
 

